# Git History Management

This repository uses the `Richard` branch as the active working branch.

Use these rules when helping manage Git history from Cursor, Codex, or a terminal.

## Safety Rules

- Never run `git reset --hard`, `git clean -fd`, or `git checkout -- <path>` unless Richard explicitly asks for destructive cleanup.
- Prefer history inspection before mutation:
  - `git status -sb`
  - `git log --oneline --decorate --graph -12`
  - `git show --stat <commit>`
  - `git diff <base>..<head>`
- Stage files explicitly. Avoid `git add -A` when generated outputs or raw data are mixed with source changes.
- Do not commit `__pycache__`, `.pyc`, virtual environments, local logs, or editor state.
- For GitHub push from this workspace, use:

```powershell
git -c http.proxy= -c https.proxy= push origin Richard
```

## Commit Style

Use short, concrete commit messages:

```text
Add ARRT Kissinger experiment method
Update PS model evaluation report
Clean generated Python caches
```

## Useful Review Questions

Before commit:

- Does the diff include only intended files?
- Are generated CSV/JSON/PNG outputs intentionally part of the record?
- Are raw DSC files intentionally being versioned?
- Did a script regenerate files deterministically?
- Was at least one relevant verification command run?

## Common Commands

```powershell
git status -sb
git log --oneline --decorate --graph -12
git show --stat HEAD
git diff --stat
git diff --cached --stat
git ls-files '*__pycache__*'
```
